! The first three things ~ the house reads its code and its work from the wiki

''The question'' (operator, 2026-11-14, quote license): //"how would you improve the workflow/token-burn? Scouting as parallel Opus spirits that write to memes for the builders to consume? The code files have grown large, and until the later dogfooding isomorphic-lift/re-org-re-factor pass it seems that reading large code files burns context... this work has become complexified with that tension AND the number of tests that grew organically and needs the same cleanup... (eventually I'll want all the code files mirrored into the live Lararium wikis, probably in the `lararium/` bag as code tiddlers with wrapping meme contexts, and that means smaller code files and more modular designs, but defer that full complex design). What would the first 3 things towards this intent can we accomplish once the next dogfood-alpha lararium stands founded?"//

''The order'' (operator, 2026-11-14, quote license, after the controller's answer drew "Pono"): //"Pono, add those three to the roadmap; Send an opus scout to design the concrete 'first 3 things' wave map, might need to define a new recipe or true-up the set of wiki recipes to all the ones in scope now. Once I restand the Lararium, I want you to write some minimal mems and memories, ensure they come back as the pono design indicates through the session start hooks and other mcp/ux calls, and then I'll stand up a new main session to take over."//

''The three things'' (approved): (1) a code map in the wiki that a tool writes, never a model; (2) the work itself as tiddlers: road items, lane cards, handbacks; (3) the rite as one runnable script, with a test ledger beside it. The road seats them as `L40`, `L41` and `L42`, and the handoff walk rides the re-founding band (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/the-order`>>).

''Register.'' Every claim here carries one of two marks: ''measured'' (read in the tree at `96b6e59a3`, 2026-11-14, with `file:line` or the instrument named) or ''inferred'' (a design reading no run has tested). Where this carrier decides, the decision reads overrulable and names its reason.

''The costs this carrier answers'' (measured with `git ls-files` over `packages/**` and `wc`; the controller's own instrument counted 1,742 source and 2,056 test files, so the two sweeps differ on what counts as a test path): 1,565 source files (1,326 TypeScript or JavaScript, 239 Python) hold 316,242 lines; 2,119 test-path files hold 298,782 lines, plus 68 files under `tests/`; ten source files run past 1,500 lines, the largest `packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts` at 4,939 lines and 363,451 bytes (about 90,000 tokens read whole); the road carrier weighs 482,515 bytes. Tokens went to a walker re-deriving the rite four times, every builder running every suite, whole-meme reads, rediscovery of what a reader already traced, and wrong-shape rounds from symptom briefs (the controller's ledger, 2026-11-14).

