!! The wikis in scope ~ the recipe true-up

Each row reads its layers top to bottom in the order `expandRecipe` lays them (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/wiki-recipe.ts`; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/recipe-layer-model#/daemon-and-domain`>>). "Mirror" names the folder the working layer projects to and whether git tracks it (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/residency-follows-the-contract#/two-workspaces`>>). The faces carry the rite's names: face 0 the steward (the Kahu chair), face 1 the engineer, face 2 the referee (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/founding-runbook#/the-three-face-rite`>>).

|! slug |! class |! recipe (top first) |! owner · seats |! mirror · git |! holds |
| `daemon` (one per face, `daemon-<F>`) | daemon | temp · working (the face's device slot) · `bags/daemon-<F>` (local canon, unsigned) · `bags/kahua-<F>` (the signed stage, lift-only) · the vessel's library bags · `bags/crossroads` · `bags/daemon` · `bags/oracle` | one face; refuses every share (`share-face-private`) | `<projections>/wikis/daemon-<F>` under the house root; no git | the face's memory memes (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/<class>/<slug>`); in the steward's, the house laws (#/the-handoff-walk) and, until `works` opens, the wave's lane cards and handbacks (#/thing-two-the-work-as-tiddlers) |
| `lares` | house canon | temp · draft · personal · working (the realm workbench, the steward's private cabal) · `bags/lares` (the Kahu realm's standing document) · the recipe's libraries · `bags/oracle` | the steward writes canon live (`requireKahuReach`); the rite seats the engineer `write` and the referee `read`, and on one vessel each seated face writes its own `personal` (the rest gate, `C2`) | the workbench in the checkout's `wikis/lares`, tracked by git; each face's `personal` under `<projections>/personal/<F>/lares`, untracked | the house's design canon: the road, the handoff meme, this map |
| `lararium` | house canon | as `lares`, its canon `bags/lararium`, and NEW: the derived library `codemap` beneath canon (decision 1 below) | as `lares` | the checkout's `wikis/lararium` once a steward write mints it (measured: `wikis/` holds `crossroads`, `elyncia`, `elyncia-referee`, `lares`, `sdm` and no `lararium` folder today); tracked | the mesh, node and runbook canon; the code map read beside it |
| `elyncia` | house canon | as `lares`, canon `bags/elyncia` | the steward; never a lane's edit (controller-handoff #/the-lane-law) | `wikis/elyncia`, tracked | the fiction layer; out of this wave's work |
| `sdm` | house canon | as `lares`, canon `bags/sdm` | the steward; never a lane's edit | `wikis/sdm`, tracked | the RPG corpus; out of this wave's work |
| `crossroads` | house canon, the public oracle plane | as `lares`; and a library in every daemon recipe | the steward | `wikis/crossroads`, tracked | the plane every face reads; a library of each daemon wiki |
| `notes` | minted (the rite's `lares wiki init notes`) | temp · draft · personal · working (the steward's realm workbench) · `bags/notes` (the catalog entry's document) · libraries · `bags/oracle` | the steward mints and owns; the rite seats the engineer `write` and the referee `read` (`personal` on one vessel until `C2`) | `<projections>/wikis/notes`, untracked | the rite's smoke tiddlers |
| `works` (NEW) | minted shared work wiki | as `notes`, canon `bags/works` | the steward (the face the controller and its spirits wear, decision 2); the engineer and referee seated `read` once `C2` lands | `<projections>/wikis/works`, untracked | lane cards, handbacks, rite reports, wave cards; a settled wave's cards promote into `bags/works` as its archive |
| `house` (NEW) | shared topic wiki, every seated face writes (NEW class) | as `notes`, canon `bags/house` | the steward owns; every face seated `write` (after `C2`, each writes the one workbench) | `<projections>/wikis/house`, untracked | the house's shared memory (`L35`, decision 3): the house laws, the standing rulings, the open ledger, once `C2` and `L17-2a` stand |
| `codemap` (NEW bag, never a wiki) | derived library (NEW class) | composes as a library into `lararium`'s recipe alone | no hand writes it; the generator's ingest wave alone | none: its bytes rest at `<LAR_ROOT>/cache/codemap/<head>/` as the wave's source, never in a tracked tree, never in `hearth/` | one tiddler per source file and per test file (#/thing-one-the-code-map) |

`elyncia-referee` stays contract-tier, off the public floor, and outside this wave (its referee recipe stays owed at rank 28 of the road).

!!! Decision 1 ~ the code map lives in a derived library composed into `lararium`, never in `bags/lararium` (overrulable)

The operator leans the `lararium` bag. ''Weighed'' (measured): `bags/lararium/meta.mem` declares `cap-tier = "public"` and `home = "repository"`, and the genesis bake and every release cut carry each public-tier bag's own snapshot (road #/the-leaps, "a contract-tier bag never rides the public floor"). A generated map there therefore lands generated files in git on every land, churns the baked genesis floor, which only a labelled `GENESIS RE-BAKE` folds (controller-handoff #/the-lane-law, canon and genesis), and lets a model-free derivative reach the promotion and offer doors meant for authored canon. ''The house's call'': a bag of its own, `codemap`, of a new class, the DERIVED LIBRARY (defined below), composed into the `lararium` recipe as a library beneath `bags/lararium`, so a reader of the `lararium` wiki sees the map beside the canon that cites it, and nothing generated ever enters git, the floor or the offering door. ''Its cost'': one meta key and three refusals in code (the bake, the offer, the export skip a derived bag), one ingest wave per land of about 2.3 MB (#/thing-one-the-code-map), and its wiki reads wait on `L17-2a`; the files on disk serve every builder from day one. The operator's later intent, code tiddlers inside `bags/lararium` with wrapping meme contexts, inverts the source of truth and stands apart from this map: the map indexes the code where it rests today and retires once code tiddlers carry their own outlines.

!!! Decision 2 ~ road items ride the road, lane cards and handbacks ride `works`, every spirit writes as the worn face (overrulable)

''Road items'' stay inside the road carrier as slot children with fields, the shape `L17-2d` already names, so a filter reprioritizes the road and no second carrier competes with #/the-order. ''Lane cards, handbacks and rite reports'' live in a minted `works` wiki under the house root: they turn over every wave, nothing in them binds once landed (git and the CHANGELOG keep what landed), and a minted wiki keeps that churn out of git and out of canon. ''Who writes'' (measured): the MCP seat marks every call as the AI seat and acts as the vessel's worn face alone (`packages/lararium-sensorium/scripts/lares_mcp.py:84-88`, `uds.SEAT_KIND = "ai"`), and the server registers in the operator's user scope (`~/.claude.json` `mcpServers.lares`, a `docker compose exec` stdio process), so every Claude session on the machine, a tasked spirit and a worktree spirit included, reaches the same seat as the same worn face; this spirit's own session listed `lares` as configured and failed to connect, since the hearth stands cleared. A spirit therefore names itself in a field (`spirit`, `model`), a designation and no proof (`F11` owes the signed channel and the Mask on `meme_put`). The steward wears for the controller's working days, so `works` mints under the steward and its writes land `working`; the engineer and the referee wear for the rite's proofs and offers, at the operator's hand. ''The bridge'': until `L17-2a` relays the tiddler door to named wikis, the cards ride the steward's daemon wiki at the same titles, where `tiddler_put` and `wiki_filter` answer today. ''Its cost'': one wear law every brief carries (no spirit switches the worn face, since a wear switch moves every session's face at once), one `wiki init works` at the walk, and a re-put of the bridge cards into `works` once `L17-2a` lands.

!!! Decision 3 ~ shared house memory lives in the `house` topic wiki; until `C2` and `L17-2a`, in the steward's daemon wiki (overrulable)

`L35` rules the reach: a face reads its own daemon wiki and every topic wiki shared to it. A topic wiki named `house` holds what every face shares (the house laws, the standing rulings, the open ledger), owned by the steward with every face seated `write`; a face's own memory stays in its daemon wiki. ''Measured blockers'': on one vessel a seated face mounts no workbench of another face's realm and writes its own `personal` (`cabal-realm` #/the-workbench, the rest gate; `C2`), so before `C2` the engineer would read none of the steward's house memory; and `wiki_filter` on `house` read `wiki-not-anchored` before every wiki stood its own engine (#390; an unreachable recipe now refuses `wiki-unreached`). So the handoff walk writes the house laws into the steward's daemon wiki first (rank 4 of the road already names that wiki), and they re-put into `house` once both items land. ''Its cost'': one carry step later, and until then the engineer's sessions read the house laws only while the steward wears.

!!! The new classes, defined, with the true-up owed to `recipe-layer-model`

''THE DERIVED LIBRARY'' (proposed text for <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/recipe-layer-model#/daemon-and-domain`>>; a later scribe applies it, this carrier edits nothing there):

* A derived library holds records ONE named tool writes as a pure function of ONE named commit of a tracked tree. Its bag's `meta.mem` declares `cap-tier = "public"`, `home = "hearth"` and a new key `derived = "<tool>"`; each record carries the commit it derives from (`head`).
* It composes only as a library, beneath the host wiki's canon (the `libraries` row), and takes no write from any hand door: `meme put`, `tiddler put`, a residency `MOVE` or `COPY` naming it, a kāpae and a lift each refuse `derived-library-read-only`.
* One road writes it: an INGEST wave whose source root the vessel grants to that bag alone (`<LAR_ROOT>/cache/<bag>/<head>/`). A wave replaces the whole bag: a title absent from the new wave retracts to absent (a reveal, never a kāpae, since nothing lies beneath its namespace).
* It never bakes into genesis, never rides a release cut, never takes an offer or a promotion, never travels in an export or a carry (each refuses or skips by `derived`), and survives a re-founding only as its cache folder, re-ingested at the next boot or the next land.
* Its titles live under one namespace the host wiki's canon never writes (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/codemap/`), so its place beneath canon shadows nothing in practice.

''THE TOPIC WIKI EVERY SEATED FACE WRITES'' (proposed text for the same slot): a domain wiki minted by one face, shared with every face of the operator seated `write`. Its recipe matches the domain column whole. Its reach law: a face reads its own daemon wiki and every topic wiki a share entry names it in (`L35`). Until the rest seals for the roster (`C2`), only the owning face writes the workbench on one vessel and every other seated face writes its own `personal`; the slot names that limit beside the class.

''The true-up owed'' (one scribe lane on `recipe-layer-model.mem` and `bag-home`'s carrier): the two class texts above; a fourth column in the layer table for the derived library; the `derived` key in the bag meta law beside `cap-tier` and `home` (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy`>>); the `daemon-and-domain` slot's list of domain wikis gaining `works` and `house` as examples of the minted and topic classes.

