<<~ ahu slot=`#/thing-one-the-code-map`>>

!! Thing one ~ the code map (road `L40`)

''What it buys.'' A builder asks the map which file holds a seam, which lines hold the function, who imports it, which memes cite it and which tests cover it, and then opens a slice by line range. Today a builder opens `open-node-vessel.ts` whole at about 90,000 tokens to find one option at line 4445 (measured: `portPolicy`'s default, `packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:4445`). The map shows where the giants split later, at no model's cost.

!!! The tiddler shape

* ''Titles'' (decision, overrulable): `lar:///ha.ka.ba/codemap` (the map's root: head, counts), `lar:///ha.ka.ba/codemap/<package>` (one per package), `lar:///ha.ka.ba/codemap/<package>/<file-key>` (one per source file) and `lar:///ha.ka.ba/codemap/test/<package>/<file-key>` (one per test file, thing three's census). The `<file-key>` writes the in-package path with `~` for `/` (`src~commands~tiddler.ts`), so a title keeps the URI law's path within four segments; the field `repo-path` carries the exact path.
* ''Fields'': `repo-path`, `package`, `lang` (`ts` · `mjs` · `py`), `lines`, `bytes`, `blob` (the git blob id), `head` (the commit the wave derives from), `exports` (a TiddlyWiki list of exported names), `imports` (a list of repo paths, and package specifiers that resolve to none), `imported-by` (repo paths), `cited-by` (meme titles), `covered-by` (test repo paths), `covered-via` (`direct` · `barrel`), `size-class` (`giant` past 1,500 lines · `large` past 800 · `small`). ''Tags'': `codemap/file`, `codemap/pkg/<package>`, `codemap/lang/<lang>`, `codemap/<size-class>`.
* ''Text'': a table of the top-level declarations with their line ranges and kinds, and the file's leading doc comment cut to its first sentence. No code body ever rides.
* ''Type'' `text/vnd.tiddlywiki`: no `$:/` title or tag, no `module-type` or `plugin-type` field, no script type, so the code-class fence (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/tiddler-verbs.ts:466-484`) never meets it.

''An example tiddler, in full'' (the shape; its numbers read off the tree at `96b6e59a3` where measured, and the declaration lines read off `grep -n function`):

```text
title: lar:///ha.ka.ba/codemap/lararium-tw5/src~tiddler-verbs.ts
repo-path: packages/lararium-tw5/src/tiddler-verbs.ts
package: lararium-tw5
lang: ts
lines: 683
head: 96b6e59a3
exports: makeWikiFilterReactor makeTiddlerGetReactor makeWikiRenderReactor makeTiddlerPutReactor makeTiddlerDeleteReactor TiddlerVerbOptions TiddlerPosition WIKI_RENDER_BYTES
imports: packages/lararium-tw5/src/filter-page.ts packages/lararium-mesh/src/family.ts
cited-by: [[lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road]] [[lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/wiki-surface-scout]]
covered-by: tests/e2e/tiddler-door.test.ts
covered-via: direct
size-class: small
tags: codemap/file codemap/pkg/lararium-tw5 codemap/lang/ts codemap/small
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

The tiddler door's six daemon verbs on the anchor.

|! lines |! kind |! name |
| 222-230 | function | wikiOf (the `wiki-not-anchored` refusal for a bag; `wiki-unreached` answers an unreachable recipe) |
| 315-356 | export function | makeWikiFilterReactor |
| 361-409 | export function | makeTiddlerGetReactor |
| 466-484 | function | refuseCodeClass (the code-class fence) |
| 515-576 | export function | makeTiddlerPutReactor |
| 577-683 | export function | makeTiddlerDeleteReactor |
```

The `imports`, `cited-by` and `covered-by` values above stand as illustrations of the shape; the generator derives the real lists.

!!! The generator

* ''One tool'': `tools/codemap.mjs --out <dir>` (default `<LAR_ROOT>/cache/codemap/<head>/`), writing one `.tid` per tiddler and a `codemap.json` index. A pure function of `git ls-files` at `HEAD`; it reads no wall clock and calls no model.
* ''The outline source'' (measured): the workspace pins `typescript@7.0.2`, the native compiler, whose package exports a JavaScript API only under `typescript/unstable/sync` (`Project`, `Program`, `Checker`, `Symbol`) and `typescript/unstable/ast` (`createScanner`, no `createSourceFile`); `ts-morph` stands nowhere in `node_modules`, and it binds the version 5 API in any case; `web-tree-sitter@0.27.1` stands in the workspace for the memetic-wikitext grammar alone, with no TypeScript grammar; `@oxc-project/types` stands without its parser. ''The house's call'': one adapter module, `tools/codemap/outline.mjs`, over `typescript/unstable/sync`, reading each file's top-level statements with their line ranges, its exports through the checker's module symbol, and its import specifiers resolved through the program; Python files outline through `python3 -I -c 'import ast'` (top-level `def` and `class` with `lineno` and `end_lineno`). A red pins the adapter (#/thing-one-the-code-map, the reds), so an unstable API break reads red at once; where the sync API cannot walk 1,565 files inside a land's budget (unmeasured), the fallback adds `oxc-parser` as a tools-only dependency.
* ''Memes that cite'' (measured instrument): `grep -rohE 'packages/[A-Za-z0-9_./-]+\.(ts|tsx|mjs|py)' bags` finds 591 distinct repo paths cited by full path; a backtick basename (`` `open-node-vessel.ts` ``) adds 768 distinct names; 37 basenames repeat across source files (`index.ts` among them). The generator resolves a full path directly, a basename only where one source file carries it, and lists an ambiguous basename on the root tiddler as `cite-ambiguous`, never guessing. `cited-by` names the meme's `title` from its first toml fence.
* ''Tests that cover'' (inferred method): the import graph of each test file through the same program; a relative import covers that file `direct`; a package specifier (`@lararium/mesh`) resolves through the package's `exports` map to a barrel, which marks every file the barrel re-exports `barrel`, and a builder reads `direct` first. Measured scale: test files carry 12,825 import lines.
* ''Regeneration'': once at each land, after the join's green run, from the landed head; and on demand in a worktree (`--out <worktree>/.codemap`, never committed). The ingest wave lands it into `codemap` where a hearth stands.

!!! Size

Measured by a structural regex over the 1,326 TypeScript and JavaScript source files (11,515 `export` lines, 5,895 `import` lines, 15,275 top-level declarations), at an estimated 350 bytes of fields per tiddler plus 70 per export, 60 per import and 45 per declaration: about 2.3 MB across 1,326 tiddlers, 1,743 bytes on average, the largest `packages/lararium-mesh/src/index.ts` (the mesh barrel) near 36 KB. The 239 Python files and the 2,187 test tiddlers of thing three add an estimated 1.5 MB (inferred). A `wiki_filter` page answers at most 32 tiddlers or 65,536 bytes (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/filter-page.ts:18-20`), so a builder's filter asks `fields` and pages by cursor.

!!! The reads ~ who runs which filter

Each runs as `wiki_filter(filter=…, recipe="lararium", fields=[…])` on the MCP seat, or `lares wiki filter '…' --recipe lararium --fields …` on the CLI, once `L17-2a` stands; before it, the same expressions run against the `.tid` folder with `rg` over fields.

* ''A builder'': `[tag[codemap/file]repo-path[packages/lararium-mesh/src/port-lease.ts]]` then `tiddler_get(…, text=false)`; who imports a seam: `[tag[codemap/file]contains:imports[packages/lararium-mesh/src/family.ts]]`; where a name lives: `[tag[codemap/file]contains:exports[makePortDoor]]`; which tests to run: `[tag[codemap/file]repo-path[<path>]get[covered-by]enlist-input[]]`.
* ''A scribe'': files a meme cites: `[tag[codemap/file]contains:cited-by[lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/cabal-realm]]`; stale citations: `[tag[codemap/file]!has[cited-by]tag[codemap/giant]]`.
* ''The controller'': where the giants stand: `[tag[codemap/giant]!nsort[lines]]`; a package's weight: `[tag[codemap/pkg/lararium-node]get[lines]sum[]]`.

!!! What blocks it today

* ''Burned by #390'': a named wiki answers through its own engine; an unreachable recipe refuses `wiki-unreached`, and `wiki-not-anchored` stays for a bag container alone.
* The code-class fence: none, by the shape above.
* The rest gate: none, since no face writes the map.
* The derived class: unbuilt; the bake, the offer and the export read no `derived` key today (inferred from the class's absence in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/bag-home.ts:50`).

!!! Reds, files, size

* Reds: `codemap-outline-lines` (a fixture file's declarations answer their exact line ranges); `codemap-pure-of-head` (two runs at one head write byte-identical folders); `codemap-cite-ambiguous` (a basename two files carry lands on the root's `cite-ambiguous`, in no file's `cited-by`); `codemap-no-body` (no tiddler text carries a line of a fixture's function body); `derived-library-read-only` (a `meme put` into `codemap` refuses); `derived-never-bakes` (a genesis bake over a scratch tree skips a `derived` bag). Controls: a repo-path citation lands on its file; a public authored bag still bakes.
* Files: new `tools/codemap.mjs`, `tools/codemap/outline.mjs`, `tools/codemap/cites.mjs`, `tools/codemap.test.mjs` (lane `L40a`, new files alone); the derived class in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/bag-home.ts`, the bake's bag walk, the offer door's bag check, the export's bag walk, and the `lararium` recipe record (lane `L40b`).
* Size: `L40a` one builder, a short lane; `L40b` one builder, a medium lane touching four doors.
* Saves (inferred, against today's measured costs): a builder's first orientation drops from opening a giant whole (90,000 tokens) to one filter page and one slice (a few thousand); a scout's "which tests cover this" stops costing a grep round; the giants' split map falls out of `size-class` and `imported-by` with no reader.

