<<~ ahu slot=`#/thing-two-the-work-as-tiddlers`>>

!! Thing two ~ the work as tiddlers (road `L41`, carrying `L17-2d`)

''What it buys.'' A scribe filters "open, wave two" and reads twelve road items instead of the road's 482 KB; a builder reads one lane card instead of a scout's whole report; the controller reads handback status lines and opens detail on demand; and a rediscovered trace stops costing a reader, since the card names the ranges a scout already read.

!!! Three tiddler kinds

''Road items'' (`L17-2d`'s shape, on the road carrier itself): a slot child per item, `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/row/<id>` (the slot law's form awaits `L17-2d`'s ruling), fields `row`, `rank`, `band` (`wave-one` · `at-the-refounding` · `wave-two` · `after`), `status` (`open` · `flying` · `landed` · `merged`), `depends-on`, `lane`, `carrier` (the meme that holds the item's law). The controller writes them by hand on the road carrier, as `L17-2d` already names.

''Lane cards'' (in `works`; the bridge: the steward's daemon wiki at the same title): `lar:///ha.ka.ba/works/lane/<wave>/<lane>`. The template rests at #/the-lane-card.

''Handbacks'' (same home): `lar:///ha.ka.ba/works/handback/<wave>/<lane>`, fields `lane`, `status-line` (the one `<<~ status "…">>` line `mixed-model-swarm#/the-shapes` asks), `head`, `ci`, `held-out`, `reds` (the red-first lines, quoted), `rulings` (canon sources the spirit decided from), `asks` (true operator asks only), `spirit`, `model`, `landed` (the land's commit, written by the join); tags `works/handback`, `works/wave/<wave>`. The text carries the story and its walk, short.

An example handback, in full (inferred shape; the commit and test names read off `git log` for `c28a77478`):

```text
title: lar:///ha.ka.ba/works/handback/carry/c8-kahua-wear
lane: c8-kahua-wear
status-line: kahua acts ride their own face's wear; the store door parks no more
head: c28a77478
ci: green at c28a77478 (the lane's suites: lararium-node kahua-door)
held-out: not read
reds: kahua-door.test.ts "a face that stands open and unworn": Error: Test timed out in 30000ms
rulings: [[lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/kahua-memory-stage]]
asks:
spirit: Carry-Mender
model: fable
tags: works/handback works/wave/carry
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

The store door hands the kahua memes the worn face, refuses a write for any other face by name, and the canon's resolve rides the bounded find.
```

!!! The doors that write and read them

* ''Write, today'' (measured doors, the hearth standing): `tiddler_put(title=…, recipe="default", fields={…}, text=…)` into the steward's daemon wiki (no `$:/` title, no code field, so the fence passes; `tiddler-verbs.ts:476-486`); or `meme_put(uri=…, text=…, recipe="works")`, which reaches a named wiki's store today (`tiddler-verbs.ts:153`, "The meme verbs read a named wiki's store today") with the fields in the meme's toml meta block.
* ''Write, after `L17-2a`'': `tiddler_put(…, recipe="works")`.
* ''Read'': a scribe's "open, wave two": `[tag[works/lane]wave[wave-two]!status[landed]sort[rank]]`; a builder's own card: `tiddler_get(title="lar:///ha.ka.ba/works/lane/wave-two/l17-2a", recipe=…)`; the controller's sweep: `[tag[works/handback]wave[wave-two]]` with `fields=["lane","status-line","head","ci","asks"]`, then one `tiddler_get` where a status line asks for more; a lane's seams: `[tag[works/lane]contains:owner-files[packages/lararium-mesh/src/port-lease.ts]]`.
* ''How a tasked spirit writes its handback today'' (measured reach, inferred act): a spirit's session inherits the user-scope `lares` server and calls `tiddler_put` as the AI seat on the worn face; a spirit whose session finds the seat unreachable (this one did) writes the same fields into its handback message, and the controller puts it. The lane card names which.

!!! What blocks it today

* ''Burned by #390'': `works` answers on the tiddler door through its own engine (an unreachable recipe refuses `wiki-unreached`).
* The rest gate (`C2`): only the steward's wear writes `works`' workbench on one vessel.
* A cold wiki's put reaches disk only once the wiki wakes (`lares wiki hold works`, by a face that holds a writer's seat there; an export names a wiki that still stands cold as `cold-wikis`).
* The road's slot law awaits a ruling before `L17-2d` writes road items.
* No provenance tells one spirit's write from another's (`F11`); the `spirit` field designates.

!!! Reds, files, size

* Reds: `lane-card-fields-round-trip` (a card put with its fields answers them whole through `tiddler_get` and through the filter); `lane-card-no-code-class` (the template's fields pass the fence); `handback-status-line-one` (a handback carrying two status lines refuses at the helper). Control: a meme put of the same card into `works` reads back through `meme_get`.
* Files: new `tools/lane-card.mjs` (writes a card or a handback through `lares tiddler put`, or prints the MCP call for a spirit; lane `L41a`, new files alone); the road carrier (`L41b` = `L17-2d`, the controller's hand).
* Saves (inferred): a builder's brief drops from a scout's report (often 20 to 60 KB) to one card under 2,000 tokens; the controller's aftermath reads N status lines instead of N handbacks; the road stops needing whole reads for "what stands open".

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/thing-three-the-rite-script-and-test-ledger`>>

!! Thing three ~ the rite script and the test ledger (road `L42`)

''What it buys.'' Four walker rounds re-derived the rite by hand, each writing throwaway keepers and probes (measured: the walker's scratch folders `rw/` and `cm/` hold `keeper.mts`, `keeper2.mts`, `wear.sh`, `L.sh`, `b6-hearth.mjs` to `b6-hearth3.mjs`, `mcp-probe.mjs`, `mcp-probe2.mjs` and dozens of logs). One script walks the runbook's rite on a scratch hearth at each merge, and a spirit reads its report instead of walking.

!!! The rite script

* ''One entry'': `tools/rite-walk.mjs [--from <step>] [--to <step>] --out <dir>`, run on the e2e harness: `openStaged` and `foundStagedHearth` (`tests/harness/instance.ts`), the staged test custody for every passphrase act (`tools/unlock-test-custody.mjs`'s `unlockTestCustody(root, "unlock", face)`), and the browser leg through Playwright with `armTestCustody` (`packages/lararium-node/dist/probes/browser-test-custody.js`), as the walker's `b6-hearth3.mjs` and `keeper.mts` already do. It refuses any root outside a scratch prefix (the walker's own guard), unsets `LAR_BAGS` and `LAR_GENESIS`, and runs under a scratch `HOME` and `LAR_ROOT`.
* ''Its steps'' bind to the runbook by line (measured at `founding-runbook.mem` as it stands): the Stand block (`:402-410`, ten commands), memory (`:417`, an MCP `meme_put` of a keyed meme), the lift (`:419`, `kahua stage`, then `kahua lift --digest` under test custody), wearing another face (`:421`), the shared workbench (`:426-428`), offer, promote, release and accept (`:433-440`), the browser leg (`:449`), and the carry across a re-founding (`:454-467`), then the read-backs (`:476`, `:478`). Each step names its runbook line, the command, the expected answer as the runbook quotes it (a `layer: working`, an `ok — 1 of 1 seats`, a `pinSource: genesis`), and an outcome.
* ''A drift witness'': each `lares …` line inside the rite's `sh` fences maps to one step, so a runbook edit that adds a command without a step reads red at the join.
* ''The report'' (`<out>/rite-report.json`, and where a hearth answers, the tiddler `lar:///ha.ka.ba/works/rite/<head>`): per step `{step, runbook, command, expect, outcome: "pass" | "fail" | "unreached", answer (the quoted line, at most 400 bytes), ms}`; fields on the tiddler `head`, `pass`, `fail`, `unreached`, `first-fail`; tags `works/rite`.
* ''What it cannot reach, and how the report names each'': a real terminal's passphrase ward (the staged custody stands in: every such step reads `pass (staged-custody)`, never a bare `pass`); `lares reset` through the host shim (`tools/lares-container.sh reset`, and `C10`'s gate on it: `unreached: host-shim`, while the script resets through the CLI's own `reset` on the scratch root); Docker and the product image (the script runs the host's built `dist`: `unreached: image`, and the ready state of rank 2 still builds and walks the image once); the browser's paper card typed back by a human (`pass (staged-custody)` through the test route); `/mcp` reconnect inside a Claude session (the script speaks the seat's stdio as `tests/e2e/tiddler-door.test.ts` does: `pass (seat-stdio)`).
* ''Cadence'': once at each merge onto the span, in the join's run, under the 600-second single-file cap the lane law grants an e2e file whose own waits exceed the default (controller-handoff #/the-lane-law, the battery); a full walk that outruns it splits by `--from`/`--to` into legs.

!!! The test ledger

* ''One census tiddler per test file'', `lar:///ha.ka.ba/codemap/test/<package>/<file-key>` in the derived `codemap` library (the same generator, a `--tests` pass): fields `repo-path`, `kind` (`unit` · `e2e` · `witness`), `guards` (the file's leading doc comment, first sentence), `covers` (source repo paths, `direct` first), `tests` (the count of `test(` and `it(` calls), `runtime-ms`, `last-red`, `head`; tags `codemap/test`, `codemap/test/<kind>`.
* ''Runtime'' (measured source): the e2e shards already write vitest JSON (`.github/workflows/e2e-shards.yml:134`, `:166`, merged at `:237` into `merged-report.json`); the unit suites in `ci.yml` write none, so a `--reporter=json` beside their default reporter stays owed, a CI edit the controller's hand makes.
* ''Last red'': the CI artifacts of red runs name failing files; the census reads the last such run for each file, and leaves the field empty where none stands, never guessing.
* ''What the census seeds'': the later test cleanup filters duplicates (`[tag[codemap/test]covers[<path>]]` with several hits and no distinct `guards`), slow files (`[tag[codemap/test]!nsort[runtime-ms]limit[20]]`) and files that never ran red.

!!! Reds, files, size

* Reds: `rite-walk-binds-every-line` (a runbook fixture with an unmapped `lares` line reads red); `rite-walk-names-unreached` (a step the script cannot reach reports `unreached` with its cause, never `pass`); `rite-walk-scratch-only` (a root outside the scratch prefix refuses before any act); `census-runtime-from-report` (a merged report's duration lands in `runtime-ms`). Controls: a passing stand step quotes the runbook's expected line; a test file absent from every report carries no `runtime-ms`.
* Files: new `tools/rite-walk.mjs`, `tools/rite-walk/steps.mjs`, `tools/rite-walk.test.mjs` (lane `L42a`, new files alone); `tools/codemap/tests.mjs` (lane `L42b`, after `L40a`); one `ci.yml` line (the controller's hand).
* Saves (inferred): each rehearsal stops spending a walker spirit's whole session (four rounds measured); a wave's join learns at merge which rite step broke, with the quoted line; the census replaces a test-cleanup scout's first sweep.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-lane-card`>>

!! The lane card ~ one builder's brief, under two thousand tokens

A scout writes it; one builder reads it and nothing else first. Fields carry what a filter reads; the text carries what a person reads.

```text
title: lar:///ha.ka.ba/works/lane/<wave>/<lane>
lane: <lane>
row: <road id>
wave: <wave>
status: open | briefed | flying | handed-back | landed | parked
head: <the commit the builder branches from>
branch: <the lane branch>
owner-files: <repo paths this lane alone edits>
open-ranges: <repo-path:first-last …, the slices to read>
leave-unread: <files or slots the builder never opens>
seams: <other lanes and the files they hold>
reds: <test names, red first>
suites: <the packages whose suites this lane runs>
depends-on: <items or lanes>
spirit: <mask name>
model: <model>
tags: works/lane works/wave/<wave>
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

''Prove'': one sentence, what stands when the lane lands.
''Start'': the harness seats a new worktree on `main`; branch from `head` first (`git switch -c <branch> <head>`), and read `git log -1` before any edit.
''Read'': the `open-ranges` alone, then the carrier slot named in `row`; open a code map tiddler before any whole file.
''Wear'': never switch the vessel's worn face; never touch the host shim, `~/.lares`, genesis or the boot seed.
''Run'': the suites of `suites` alone; the join runs everything once.
''Hand back'': one handback tiddler (or its fields in the message where the seat stands unreachable).
```

!!! A worked card ~ wave two's `L17-2a`

The ranges read off the tree at `96b6e59a3` (measured).

```text
title: lar:///ha.ka.ba/works/lane/wave-two/l17-2a
lane: l17-2a
row: L17-2a
wave: wave-two
status: open
head: <the span head the controller names at launch>
branch: lane/l17-2a-relay
owner-files: packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts packages/lararium-mesh/src/vessel-island-pool-core.ts packages/lararium-mesh/src/port-lease.ts
open-ranges: packages/lararium-mesh/src/port-lease.ts:1-115 packages/lararium-mesh/src/vessel-island-pool-core.ts:275-290 packages/lararium-mesh/src/vessel-island-pool-core.ts:375-430 packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:380-390 packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:4435-4455 packages/lararium-tw5/src/tiddler-verbs.ts:150-200
leave-unread: open-node-vessel.ts beyond the two ranges; record-port.ts (L17-2b alone edits it); every bags/ carrier but wiki-surface-scout#/phases
seams: L17-2b holds record-port.ts and record-port-handler.ts; C1's second cut holds the dial and gate legs; C2 holds operator-daemon-behavior.ts
reds: wiki-filter-named-wiki-engine relay-lease-from-session-face relay-second-face-refuses
suites: lararium-mesh lararium-node lararium-tw5, and tests/e2e/tiddler-door.test.ts alone under the 600-second cap
depends-on: the standing hearth for its walk
spirit: <mask>
model: <model>
tags: works/lane works/wave/wave-two
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

''Prove'': `wiki_filter` and `tiddler_get` answer a named wiki (`notes`) through a width-`none` port under a lease minted from the session's face, and a second face's lease refuses.
''Start'': branch from `head`; the default port policy reads at `open-node-vessel.ts:4445` (`faceId: wornGateFace()?.personaGroup ?? islandKey`, `edits: false`); the anchor's refusal reads at `tiddler-verbs.ts:150-160`.
''Read'': the ranges above, then wiki-surface-scout #/phases, phase 2.
''Wear'': never switch the worn face; the e2e stages its own two faces.
''Run'': the three packages' suites and the one e2e file.
''Hand back'': `lar:///ha.ka.ba/works/handback/wave-two/l17-2a`.
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-wave-map`>>

!! The wave map ~ the first-three wave, beside wave two

The lanes below own new files alone, except `L40b`, so each takes a free slot beside wave two under the road's rule (a free slot takes the lowest open rank whose files no flying lane holds), and four lanes fly at most (controller-handoff #/the-lane-law). Each builder runs the suites of the packages it touched; the join runs everything once. Every brief says: the harness seats a new worktree on `main`, and a builder branches from the named head first.

|! order |! lane |! item |! owns |! waits on |! parallel with |
| 1 | `L42a` the rite script | `L42` | `tools/rite-walk.mjs`, `tools/rite-walk/`, its test (new) | nothing (a scratch hearth) | every wave-two lane; it then runs at each of their merges |
| 1 | `L40a` the code map generator | `L40` | `tools/codemap.mjs`, `tools/codemap/`, its test (new) | nothing | `L42a`, wave two |
| 1 | `L41a` the lane-card helper | `L41` | `tools/lane-card.mjs`, its test (new) | the standing hearth for its walk | `L42a`, `L40a`, wave two |
| 2 | `L42b` the test census | `L42` | `tools/codemap/tests.mjs` (new); one `ci.yml` reporter line by the controller's hand | `L40a`'s output shape | wave two |
| 3 | `L40b` the derived library | `L40` | `bag-home.ts`, the bake's bag walk, the offer's bag check, the export's bag walk, the `lararium` recipe record | `L40a`; its wiki reads wait on `L17-2a`; no file overlap with wave two's named files (inferred: re-check `C3`'s seed-source files at launch) | `C9`, `C10`, `L17-2b` |
| 4 | `L41b` road items (`L17-2d`) | `L41` | the road carrier, the controller's hand | the slot law's ruling | any |
| 5 | the bridge's move | `L41` | no code: a re-put of the daemon-bridge cards into `works`, and of the house laws into `house` | `L17-2a` and `C2` | any |

''Beside wave two'' (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/the-order`>>): wave two's four builders (`C1`'s second cut, `C2`, `C9`, `C10`) and its two relay lanes (`L17-2a`, `L17-2b`) hold product files; `L42a`, `L40a` and `L41a` hold new tool files and fly in the same window when a slot frees. `L42a` lands first, since every later merge of wave two then reads its rite report. `L17-2a` unlocks both the code map's wiki reads and the cards' move into `works`; `C2` unlocks every face's write of `works` and `house`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-handoff-walk`>>

!! The handoff walk ~ what the outgoing controller does on the fresh hearth before a new main session takes over

As of 2026-11-14 the span's head carries the burn-and-sweep pass under a labelled genesis re-bake, and the hearth stands cleared and unfounded, awaiting the operator's founding; the walk follows the founding (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff#/state`>>).

Each step names the call, the answer expected, and a mark: ''day one'' (reachable on the freshly founded hearth), or ''after <item>''.

!!! What the wake hook prints, and what stays owed

''Built'' (road `L43`; `packages/lares-cli/.claude-plugin/hooks/lares-wake-hook.mjs` over `lares-wake-core.mjs`, registered as a `SessionStart` hook in the operator's `~/.claude/settings.json` with a 15-second timeout, and as the plugin's own `hooks/hooks.json`): the wake starts three reads together under one 12-second budget, the container's observation (`tools/lares-container.sh vessel stand --observe --json`), the memory index (`wiki filter '[tag[stage/index]]' --recipe default --fields title,description --limit 32 --max-bytes 4096 --json` through the shim) and the homes line (`lares home read --brief`), and emits one `additionalContext` string: the observation frame, `Lares homes: <the brief line>`, then `Lares memory index: <N> rows`, one line per meme (`title — description`) and the call that reads further. A fault prints `memory index unread: <cause>`; a vessel that answers no "up" skips the index read and says so once; a read still open at the budget stops and reports itself. `lares-compact-hook.mjs` rides `PreCompact` and hands the compaction the index and the memes in play by address (the open ledger, the standing orders), and the wake that fires on a session start of source `compact` adds the same memes-in-play line.

''Owed'' (road `L44`): the operator's one `lares home tend` after the merge, which seats the compaction hook and lifts every host hook command that names a script in the house's hooks folder which no `[[home]]` entry of the reality tunnel declares; every other hand's command stays, and a second tend writes nothing (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/cli/reality-tunnel`>>). Also owed: the real shim's answer inside `docker compose exec`, and one live session's wake and compaction witnessed.

!!! The checklist

# ''The hearth answers'' (day one): `tools/lares-container.sh vault status` names the steward worn; `/mcp` reconnects; `wiki_status(recipe="default")` answers the daemon wiki's layers with `working` writable.
# ''The house laws'' (day one): first `meme_get(uri="lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/house-laws", recipe="default")`, since `projections/` survives a re-founding and a seed may already have adopted a house-laws meme from the former steward's folder; it answers `null` on a hearth that holds none, else a text whose `canonicalHash` rides the put as `base` (a put with no base replaces the meme whole; a base the records moved past refuses as a conflict). Then `meme_put(uri="lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/house-laws", recipe="default", text=…)` with `uri-path = "ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/house-laws"` in its toml meta block and tags `stage/semantic stage/index`, into the steward's daemon wiki (`stage/index` stands proposed here as the tag of the one cold-boot view `L11` asks for). The address and the path agree: a put of that carrier at `…/kahua/memory/House/Laws` refuses `stage-path-shape` and lands nothing. The meme carries the operator's seven laws verbatim (2026-11-13): no backwards compatibility in early alpha; idempotent by intent; isomorphic by intent; no global now; causal islands; pattern integrities; talk story as Gaia-2026 and Elyncia-5492 user-story myths and surface only what survives (Mu it, talk it out, decide, record the call as overrulable). Expect a receipt with `decision: "ingest"` and `bag` naming the working layer; the same put again answers `noop`; a stage meme at a path that reads no one or two lowercase segments refuses `stage-path-shape`.
# ''The standing rulings'' (day one): one meme each, `lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/ruling/2026-11-13` and `…/ruling/2026-11-14`, tagged `stage/semantic stage/index`, each quoting the operator verbatim and pointing at the road's #/rulings for the full text.
# ''The open ledger and standing orders'' (day one): `lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/state/open-ledger` (the open φ and the lanes in flight) and `…/state/standing-orders` (the lane law's headlines: no stash, no push of the span or `main`, no `~/.lares` reads by spirits, the build lock, one battery per batch), tagged `stage/working stage/index`.
# ''Where things live'' (day one): `lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/reference/where-things-live`, tagged `stage/reference stage/index`: the road (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road`, #/the-order first), the handoff meme (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff`, #/state), this map, and the bridge cards' prefix `lar:///ha.ka.ba/works/`.
# ''The lift'' (day one, the operator's hand): `kahua_stage(title=<the house-laws meme>, text=…)`, then at a terminal `lares kahua lift <title> --face 0 --taint none`, the meme digest's first 8 hex typed back and the passphrase. Expect the meme in `kahua_list()` with `status: "standing"` (the lift stays unwalked on the hearth of 2026-11-14, so this expectation stands unmeasured).
# ''Read back through the MCP seat, cold'' (day one, a second Claude session): `wiki_filter(filter="[tag[stage/index]]", recipe="default", fields=["title","description"])` answers the six memes (the house laws, the two rulings, the open ledger, the standing orders, where things live) with a cursor (`after`) only where more than 32 stand; `tiddler_get(title=<a meme>, recipe="default", text=false)` answers fields alone with `bag` naming the working layer; `meme_get(uri="lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/house-laws", recipe="default")` answers the text. `kahua_list()` answers no items for memes the meme door wrote on a fresh steward (measured 2026-11-14 on the hearth founded on `d9c96f525`; road `C17`), so it proves nothing here before the lift.
# ''Read back through the CLI'' (day one): `tools/lares-container.sh wiki filter '[tag[stage/index]]' --recipe default --json` and `tools/lares-container.sh tiddler get <title> --skinny --recipe default --json` answer the same memes and fields; `tiddler get` with no `--recipe default` refuses `no-container`.
# ''Read back on disk'' (day one): each meme's file under `<projections>/wikis/daemon-<F>/`, read by the operator (spirits read nothing under `~/.lares`).
# ''Read back in the browser'' (after `L4f`): a joined own-hearth page mounts the daemon document only once `L4f` widens the admit carriage; until then the page shows the floor and the shared wikis, never the daemon memes.
# ''Read back at wake'' (after the operator's one `lares home tend`, road `L44`): a new session's `SessionStart` context carries `Lares memory index: 6 rows` and a line per meme. The wake's index read needs no config act and rides the merged tree; the tend seats the compaction hook and lifts each host hook command that names a house hook script no `[[home]]` entry declares, printing `lifted <scripts> from <path> (<id>)` per hook file (`claude.hooks-owned`, `codex.hooks-owned`, `copilot.hooks-owned`); before it, `lares home read --brief` names those items beside `lares home tend`.
# ''A restart'' (day one): `tools/lares-container.sh down`, then `up` (the passphrase at the terminal), then step 7 again answers the same memes and hashes.
# ''A re-wear'' (day one): `lares vault unlock --face 1`, `wiki_filter(…)` answers the engineer's own daemon wiki and none of the steward's memes (reach law); `lares vault unlock --face 0` and the memes answer again.
# ''The works wiki'' (day one for the mint, at the operator's terminal; after `L17-2a` for its filter): `tools/lares-container.sh wiki init works` wearing the steward, since the seat's `wiki` tool carries `switch`, `hold`, `release` and `active` and mints nothing; then `wiki(verb="hold", slug="works")` or `lares wiki hold works`, and the first bridge card put into the steward's daemon wiki at `lar:///ha.ka.ba/works/lane/…`.
# ''The house wiki'' (after `C2` and `L17-2a`): `lares wiki init house`, `lares wiki share house --write 'joshua-fontany-engineer joshua-fontany-referee' --face 0` (the names ride as a title list, `share-cmd.ts:30-39`), the house-law memes re-put there, and the engineer's `wiki_filter(…, recipe="house")` answers them.

!!! The new session's first turn, in order

# The boot seed (CLAUDE.md seats it) and the wake's context.
# `wiki_filter(filter="[tag[stage/index]]", recipe="default", fields=["title","description"])`, then `meme_get` of the house laws and the where-things-live meme.
# The road's #/the-order, then `controller-handoff` #/state, then this map's #/the-wave-map.
# `git log --oneline -10` on the span, against the handoff's heads.

''Questions for the outgoing controller while it still answers'': which lanes fly and at which heads; which flat memories stay unmoved and why; whether the steward stays the worn face for the controller's days (decision 2); which rite steps the last rehearsal walked by hand and which only the script reached; which of the open items below it would overrule.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/open`>>

!! Open ~ each with a default

* ''The code map's home'' (decision 1): a derived `codemap` library in the `lararium` recipe. Default: as decided; the operator's lean toward `bags/lararium` waits for the code-tiddler era, where authored code tiddlers replace the map.
* ''The file-key form'': `~` for `/` inside one path segment. Default: as decided; `repo-path` carries the exact path for every filter.
* ''The outline source under TypeScript 7'': the `unstable/sync` API, unmeasured at 1,565 files. Default: the adapter over it, with `oxc-parser` as the named fallback.
* ''The worn face for AI days'' (decision 2): the steward. Default: the steward; the engineer wears only for the rite's offers and proofs.
* ''The road's slot law for `L17-2d`'': a ruling owed before road items carry fields. Default: `#/row/<id>` slot children on the road carrier.
* ''The bridge's move'': daemon-wiki cards re-put into `works`, then kāpae'd in the daemon wiki once each receipt stands. Default: re-put, never a residency `MOVE`, since the daemon working layer refuses every share.
* ''The house wiki's name'': `house`. Default: `house`, a plain word every face reads.
* ''The unit suites' JSON reporter'': a `ci.yml` edit. Default: the controller's hand, in `L42b`'s window.
